    "q-143751": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143751",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{10}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{4}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{4}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{10}+{1}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
