    "q-143794": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143794",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.25$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{3}\\cdot 0.05+{1}^{3}\\cdot 0.4+{2}^{3}\\cdot 0.1+{3}^{3}\\cdot 0.2+{4}^{3}\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.05+1\\cdot 0.4+8\\cdot 0.1+27\\cdot 0.2+64\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0+0.4+0.8+5.4+16 \\\\  & =22.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
